header: ['| ID | Date | Decided by | Decision | Rationale / evidence | Reopen if |', '| D-053 | 2026-10-01 | delivery-orchestrator | **DG1 round-7 repairs (both DG1 round-6 findings Low/non-mandatory): close the concrete native-loader route and formally STATE+ACCEPT the irreducible residual of the module lint, so the denylist does not churn a finding per round.** (1) **F-DG1-127 (code-security): two loader routes outside `LOADER_BUILTINS`.** A1 `node:sqlite` `DatabaseSync(...,{allowExtension:true}).loadExtension(so)` loads a native shared object — the same class as the `process.dlopen` route closed by F-DG1-125. A2 runtime code GENERATION then a dynamic import of a literal same-module path (`writeFileSync(new URL("./gen.mjs",…)); await import("./gen.mjs")`) — the specifier is a legal own-module path and the bytes exist only at runtime, so the lint never sees them. **Fix (T-DG1-BE8):** add `sqlite`/`node:sqlite` to `LOADER_BUILTINS` (a module never needs SQLite — persistence is `@mth/db`/PostgreSQL, ADR-0003; zero imports in src), closing A1 (self-check A1 added). A2 and the general class are **documented and ACCEPTED as stated residuals** in the testkit header, NOT chased: (a) the pre-existing runtime-data-flow residual; (b) runtime code-generation-then-import (node:fs deliberately not banned — tests and future modules legitimately read files; a write-API-only ban is brittle); (c) the loader/eval denylist is ENUMERATED and cannot be proven exhaustive over every host capability (a future Node built-in, `WebAssembly` instantiation) — **known native loaders are closed as found** (`process.dlopen` F-DG1-125, `node:sqlite` F-DG1-127). Rationale: this lint is static defence-in-depth for the ADR-0002 module boundaries, enforced against human-reviewed code that runs with a read-only production source tree — **not** a runtime security boundary; the residuals are accepted, not syntactically closable. (2) **F-DG1-212 (qa): the REQ-DLV-042 cited installer acceptance log was the pre-F-DG1-126 13-case run.** Regenerated `docs/delivery/test-evidence/DG1/orchestrator/install-sandbox-acceptance.log` against the post-fix installer: AC-1..AC-10, 14 passed, 0 failed, exit 0. | DG1 round 6: all three reviewers PASS on candidate `sha256:a7b46fbc…`; the only open items were these two Low/non-mandatory findings. CLAUDE.md (a control\'s stated guarantee must hold; evidence must match the frozen candidate). **Evidence:** `architecture.test.ts` 78/78 incl. self-check A1 + the real module-tree check; `@mth/api` typecheck/eslint/prettier clean; the regenerated 14/14 installer log; the round-7 freeze + its three PASS reviews + auditor. | A reviewer demonstrates a native/loader route that a module could reach and that is NOT a stated residual (then it is closed like sqlite); or a module legitimately needs `node:fs`/`node:sqlite` (then the ban/residual is revisited). |']
